hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1055","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He prayed with us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, five times, so we said, O Messenger of God, has anything happened in prayer? He said: No, we said: You led such-and-such with us. He said: “I am only human. I forget just as you forget, so if one of you forgets, let him prostrate two prostrations.” Then he, may God bless him and grant him peace, turned and prostrated two times."
"1056","It was narrated by Bundar, it was narrated by Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, Al-Hakam narrated to me, H, Abu Musa narrated to us, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: It was narrated to us by Abd al-Rahman. We told Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Bundar told us, Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, Sa’id told us Ibn Amir, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, H. Ahmad Ibn Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli and Muhammad Ibn Yahya Al-Quti’ narrated to us, saying: They narrated to us Muhammad bin Bakr, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mughirah, both on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He prayed the noon prayer with five days, and a man from among the people said to him: Should I add more prayers? He said: What is that? They said: I prayed five times. He said: So he prostrated two times. After he greeted him.” This is the hadith of Muhammad bin Bakr"
"1057","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Al-Nadhar bin Shumail told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah. On the authority of Abdullah: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed five times, and it was said to him: Should I add more to the prayer? He said: No, then he prostrated two prostrations."
